    InstalledComponent { seen: seen_unordered(), component: e1_j30, terminals: names(ns: e1_j30_points), identification: MarkingUnresolved { marking: Absent, discriminator: "a three-position header silkscreened J30 beside U41 and D7_P2 (bench-session upload 2304eac4; J31, beside Q530, is another header): which of A, B, C the operator's 'pin 1' and 3.1 V point were, and each position to J20's black lead unpowered on a recorded range against the baseline" } },
    // No terminal of U49 was ever probed. The sixteen TI pin names that used to sit in this field came
    // from lv165a_pins, which is TI's numbering for the SN74LV165A: a fact about the PART. Written onto a
    // specimen it made the datasheet a second authority for what the specimen is, and unlike a pin role it
    // survived the identification being only a candidate. The bench probed nothing here, so nothing is
    // claimed; TI's names are reachable through identified_row(c) when the marking settles.
